meta {
  name: Google OAuth Single Sign-On
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "credential": "google_oauth_client_credential_token",
    "role": "founder"
  }
}

docs {
  # Google OAuth Single Sign-On
  Sign in or register automatically using a verified Google Account credential token.

  ### Authentication
  Public (Google ID token / client payload)

  ### Allowed Roles
  - Guest

  ### Request Body Fields
  - `credential` (string, required) - Google ID token or OAuth response credential.
  - `role` (string, optional) - Requested role if creating a new user.

  ### Response Status Codes
  - `200` - Google sign-in verified and session created.
  - `400` - Invalid Google credential token.
  - `403` - Account is currently suspended or awaiting approval.
  - `500` - Internal server error.

  ### Response Example (200)
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "user": {
      "id": "usr_google_01",
      "name": "Rohan Verma",
      "email": "rohan.verma@gmail.com",
      "role": "founder",
      "avatar": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/sample-avatar"
    }
  }
  ```
}
